Keep a shared code as empty text.
Place "<DIV>This is the first line <![CDATA[<div>]]></DIV>" into code.
Keep a shared spot as 0.
Keep a shared ok as 0.
Keep a shared name as empty text.
Keep a shared found as 0.
Keep a shared tags as an empty list of text.
Set ok to 1.

To findmark from cursor (a whole number).
Set found to 0 minus 1.
Repeat while cursor plus 2 is at most the last position of code.
The piece is the slice of code from cursor to cursor plus 3.
If piece matches "]]>", set found to cursor, stop.
Add 1 to cursor.

To takecdata.
If found is less than 0, set ok to 0, return.
Set spot to found plus 3.

To scan from cursor (a whole number).
If cursor is more than the last position of code, set spot to cursor, return.
The here is cursor.
If character here of code is ">", set spot to cursor, return.
Place character here of code into name.
Scan from cursor plus 1.

To approve.
The size is the number of characters in name.
If size is less than 1, set ok to 0.
If size is more than 9, set ok to 0.
For every index from 0 to size minus 1.
The letter is the slice of name from index to index plus 1.
If letter comes before "A", set ok to 0.
If "Z" comes before letter, set ok to 0.

To closetag.
Add 2 to spot.
Set name to empty text.
Scan from spot.
If spot is more than the last position of code, set ok to 0, return.
Add 1 to spot.
Approve.
If ok is 0, return.
The depth is the number of items in tags.
If depth is 0, set ok to 0, return.
The top is item (depth minus 1) of tags.
If name does not match top, set ok to 0, return.
Remove the last item from tags.

To opentag.
The start is the slice of code from spot to spot plus 1.
The angle is 0.
If start matches "<", set angle to 1.
If angle is 0, set ok to 0, return.
Add 1 to spot.
Set name to empty text.
Scan from spot.
If spot is more than the last position of code, set ok to 0, return.
Approve.
If ok is 0, return.
Add 1 to spot.
The copy is a copy of name.
Place copy into tags.
Content.

To content.
Repeat while spot is at most the last position of code and ok is 1.
The here is spot.
The finish is the last position of code.
The marker is the slice of code from here to here plus 1.
The next is here plus 1.
If next is more than finish, set next to finish.
The near is next plus 1.
If near is more than finish plus 1, set near to finish plus 1.
The follower is the slice of code from next to near.
The wide is here plus 9.
If wide is more than finish, set wide to finish plus 1.
The head is the slice of code from here to wide.
The cdata is 0.
If head matches "<![CDATA[", set cdata to 1.
If cdata is 1, findmark from here plus 9.
If cdata is 1, takecdata.
The isangle is 0.
If marker matches "<", set isangle to 1.
The isclose is 0.
If follower matches "/", set isclose to 1.
If cdata is 0 and isangle is 0, add 1 to spot.
If cdata is 0 and isangle is 1 and isclose is 1, closetag.
If cdata is 0 and isangle is 1 and isclose is 1, stop.
If cdata is 0 and isangle is 1 and isclose is 0, opentag.

The size is the number of characters in code.
If size is less than 1, set ok to 0.
If size is more than 0 and ok is 1, opentag.
If spot is not size, set ok to 0.
The depth is the number of items in tags.
If ok is 1 and depth is 0, show true, otherwise show false.
